  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "ourYjj+50mpl3/qjXRJn8i8PPUw=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:35:32.000Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "Powerhouse packages follow a standard publishing workflow:\n\n1. **Package naming**: Scoped convention `@your-org-ph/your-package-name` (the `-ph` suffix identifies Powerhouse ecosystem packages)\n2. **powerhouse.manifest.json**: Declares package contents - document models (with document type IDs) and editors (linked to document types). Before the first publish, set its `name`, `description`, and `publisher`, and make `package.json`'s `name` match\n3. **Build**: `pnpm build` or `npm run build` compiles to dist/\n4. **Publish**: `npm login` then `npm publish` (with `\"publishConfig\": { \"access\": \"public\" }` for scoped packages), or `ph publish --registry=<url>`\n5. **Install**: `ph install @your-org-ph/your-package-name` makes document models and editors available in any Powerhouse environment\n\n`ph install` defaults to the **Powerhouse registry**: it only registers the package in `powerhouse.config.json` with provider `\"registry\"`, and Connect loads it from the registry CDN at runtime -- it does NOT install into `node_modules` by default. Use `--local` to also install into `node_modules` (provider `\"local\"`) so `ph connect build` bundles it and the preview works without the registry being reachable. Registry URL resolution order: `--registry` flag > `PH_REGISTRY_URL` env > `powerhouse.config.json` > default.\n\nThe scaffolded `package.json` `files` array contains only `[\"/dist\"]` -- the compiled build output is what ships, not the source `document-models` / `editors` folders.\n\nSemantic versioning is used for package versions. The AGPL-3.0-only license is common in the ecosystem.\n\n_Corrected 2026-08-13 against Powerhouse v6.2.2-dev.45._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-14T12:35:32.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:35:32.000Z"
    }
  },
